Bioinformatics Engineer","Senior Bioinformatics Engineer","Computational Biology Platform Lead"]},{"type":"h","text":"PhD directions"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential research areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Computational Biology"},{"text":"Bioinformatics"},{"text":"Genomics"},{"text":"Computational Genomics"},{"text":"Structural Bioinformatics"},{"text":"Systems Biology"},{"text":"Cancer Genomics"},{"text":"Population Genomics"},{"text":"Single-Cell Genomics"},{"text":"Transcriptomics"},{"text":"Proteomics"},{"text":"Metagenomics"},{"text":"Computational Drug Discovery"},{"text":"AI for Biology"},{"text":"Protein Structure Prediction"},{"text":"Biological Data Science"},{"text":"Precision Medicine"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2040–2046 evolution"},{"type":"p","text":"The Bioinformatics Analyst of the future will increasingly work with multi-omics, single-cell data, spatial biology, large-scale genomic databases, AI foundation models and cloud-scale biological computing. The role can evolve from simply analysing datasets into designing reproducible computational systems and AI-driven biological discovery platforms."},{"type":"h","text":"Strong long-term profile:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Genetic Engineering","Bioinformatics","Python/R","Statistics","Genomics","Cloud","AI/ML"],"sep":"+"}]}]}